---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description:
		"About Ali Fadda — senior software backend engineer working across NestJS, Temporal, and AI products.",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-6">About</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			I'm <strong>Ali Fadda</strong>, a senior software backend engineer. Most of my work lives in
			TypeScript and Node — NestJS services, event-driven systems, and lately AI product surfaces
			built on Temporal, LLMs, and RAG.
		</p>
		<p>
			I like taking ambiguous product goals and turning them into shipped systems: clear APIs,
			observable workflows, and interfaces that don't hide the hard parts.
		</p>
		<h2>What I care about</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>Backend systems that stay understandable under growth</li>
			<li>Clean architecture and domain modeling when complexity earns it</li>
			<li>AI features that are useful in production, not just demos</li>
			<li>Mentoring and raising the quality bar with the people around me</li>
		</ul>
		<h2>Recently</h2>
		<p>
			At Creativo I worked across AI media pipelines, social/ad automation, landing page generation,
			and a brand RAG assistant. Before that I built backend systems at Boxit, VIWELL, and Taager —
			Kafka, PostgreSQL, AWS, payments, and performance work that moved the needle.
		</p>
		<p>
			Want the full timeline? See the <a href="/resume">resume</a> — it's generated from a single
			Markdown source so updates stay in sync.
		</p>
		<p>
			Reach me at
			<a href="mailto:contact@alifadda.me">contact@alifadda.me</a>
			or
			<a href="https://linkedin.com/in/alifadda" rel="noreferrer" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
